<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  GameConditionDefs_DarkAurora.xml   RimStarWars: Weather Suite   2026-09-01
  ============================================================================
  WEATHER_SUITE_SLICE_1, unit 2 — dark-side auroras. Doc §5: "the ONE
  nightside weather event with zero cost... a genuine morale/mood buff for
  pawns who witness it outdoors... a navigation aid: aurora-lit terrain
  grants a partial sight-range restoration."

  Owner's ruling (RULED table, saved 2026-09-02): "use the Aurora graphic
  effect but maximized in brightness and color." conditionClass points at
  RimMandrake.StarWars.WeatherSuite.GameCondition_DarkAuroraMax
  (WeatherSuiteHook.cs) — a subclass of vanilla GameCondition_Aurora that
  overrides only SkyTarget() to push color-lerp strength and sky glow to
  their maximum; everything else (color cycling, mood buff, ExposeData) is
  inherited unchanged. It still does exactly what the doc's §5 asks: +14
  mood via its paired ThoughtDef (below), and now a maximized sky glow,
  which on an otherwise near-zero-visibility nightside map IS the sight-range
  restoration the doc asks for — RimWorld's own sight/visibility math
  already scales off ambient glow, so no separate new mechanic is needed
  for that half of the doc's ask either.

  What IS new: RSW_WS_DarkAurora is a SEPARATE GameConditionDef from
  vanilla's own `Aurora` (never touched), fired by its own IncidentDef via
  IncidentWorker_NightsideAurora (WeatherSuiteHook.cs), which requires a
  player-home map in the RimUtinni geometry def's nightside band before it
  can fire — vanilla Aurora stays available everywhere, unmodified; this is
  purely additive.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef>
    <defName>RSW_WS_DarkAurora</defName>
    <label>dark-side aurora</label>
    <description>The deep night has no sun, but it is not without light. A magnetospheric aurora is lighting the sky — the one beauty this hemisphere owns for free.</description>
    <allowUnderground>false</allowUnderground>
    <canAffectAllPlanetLayers>true</canAffectAllPlanetLayers>
    <canBePermanent>false</canBePermanent>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.StarWars.WeatherSuite.GameCondition_DarkAuroraMax</conditionClass>
    <endMessage>The dark-side aurora is fading.</endMessage>
    <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
    <letterText>A dark-side aurora is lighting up the night sky. It will boost the mood of anyone outside to see it, and brighten the ground enough to see by.</letterText>
    <silencedByConditions>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">UnnaturalDarkness</li>
    </silencedByConditions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
